# Tessera stdlib: B128Extended and the B128 helpers built on it
#
# B128Extended is a 192-bit-mantissa float. Code here computes in it and rounds once to B128. The 79 bits
# beyond B128's 113 absorb the rounding of every intermediate step (each at most 2^-190 relative) and the
# truncation of the series, so the results are faithful: within 1 ulp, and almost always the correctly rounded
# value. The method follows RazorForge's B128Math and TLFloat (Naoki Shibata, Boost 1.0). The series
# coefficients and constants below were computed to 192 bits with exact rationals and mpmath. The correctly
# rounded exp, ln, sin, cos, the atan family, cbrt, hypot, and sqrt are CORE-MATH ports, methods defined in
# their own files of this folder.

module Standard/System/Numerics/B128

